    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d341">

                <pb facs="0332" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 P.W./571: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Hanoi</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanoi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-17T16:00:00+07:00">October 17, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 18—2:59 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>159. Reference to my telegram No. 157, October 14, 11 a.m. According to
                    reasonably reliable sources, the Japanese have landed approximately 2,000 troops
                    at Haiphong within the last 24 hours. I am also informed that the Japanese have
                    recently requested that the Government General allow them to organize and manage
                    the railway transportation of Japanese troops throughout Indochina, a request
                    which has been refused up to now. The news of the resignation of the Konoye
                        Government<anchor n="10" xml:id="d341-f1"/> has increased appreciably the
                    apprehension here of further Japanese moves in this area.</p>
                <p>Sent to Cavite for repetition to the Department, Chungking, Pei-ping, Hong Kong,
                    Shanghai. Shanghai please repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d341-f1" n="10" xml:id="d341-f1-content">
                <p>Concerning the fall of the Japanese Cabinet, see telegram No. 1643, October 16, 9
                    p.m., from the Ambassador in Japan, <ref target="frus1941v04#pg_511">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iv</hi>, p. 511</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
